Subject: Cantor Service-Backed MCP

Description: Optional resident-service execution for the unchanged one-tool read-only Cantor MCP adapter, with a pinned authenticated service client, startup readiness proof, exact ProtocolResponse projection, and embedded rollback.

@ [source] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-07-29_cantor_service_backed_mcp_activation\Dictated_Cantor_Service_Backed_MCP_Activation_Source.sop
@ [manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-07-29_cantor_service_backed_mcp_activation\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Service_Backed_MCP.exploded.sop
@ [existing_MCP] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Read_Only_MCP_Adapter_Profile.sop
@ [resident_service] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Resident_Service.sop

& [CanonicalIdentity] is the bounded backend-extension authority
  + [canonical_specification_uuid] is 27a60f5b-4572-4b40-98bf-ec27cf44e0aa
  + [service_profile] is cantor-resident-service/0.1
  + [adapter_profile] is cantor-mcp-adapter/0.1
  + [tool_set] is exactly query_sop
  + [effect_boundary] is read_only
  + [status] is authorized

& [BackendSelection] is strict process startup
  + [embedded] is exactly --environment plus one path
  + [resident] is exactly --service-config plus one absolute path
  = must: reject missing, duplicate, mixed, or unknown startup arguments
  = must: preserve embedded behavior without semantic or schema change

& [ResidentServiceClient] is pinned process-lifetime transport state
  + [construction] is complete strict service configuration and capability loading once
  + [pinned] is loopback address, frame bound, read timeout, write timeout, and capability
  + [startup_probe] is one authenticated Status operation before MCP STDIO service begins
  + [request_identity] is the unchanged inner ProtocolRequest request_id
  + [execution] is one authenticated Execute operation
  = must: verify service protocol and response request identity
  = must: exclude capability from Debug, faults, MCP content, and arguments
  - never: reread changed client configuration during a running MCP process

& [ProjectionContract] is exact
  + [success] is ServiceDisposition Success with ServiceResult Protocol
  + [structured_content] is the nested unchanged ProtocolResponse
  + [semantic_error] is the nested ProtocolResponse with its original status, exit class, faults, proof, and continuation
  + [service_error] is a bounded adapter fault with service code and stage but no fabricated semantic response
  + [unexpected_result] is a bounded adapter fault
  = must: retain the existing output schema, concise text summary, and MCP error marking

& [RefreshContract] is fail-closed visibility
  + [service] may atomically activate a new generation under resident-service authority
  + [MCP] performs no refresh and owns no activation policy
  + [old_request] against a new generation returns the exact core trust or binding failure
  + [new_request] with supervisor-issued new bindings may succeed without MCP restart
  - never: repair stale environment or package expectations

& [ToolBoundary] is unchanged
  + [published_tools] is one query_sop
  + [model_callable_lifecycle] is none
  + [model_callable_configuration] is none
  + [model_callable_secrets] is none
  = must: keep annotations read_only, non_destructive, idempotent, and closed_world

& [RequirementSet] is traceable
  + [SBM-001] is strict mutually exclusive startup
  + [SBM-002] is pinned authenticated service client and startup readiness
  + [SBM-003] is exact cross-path ProtocolResponse equality
  + [SBM-004] is real live cantord plus MCP STDIO proof
  + [SBM-005] is refresh visibility with old-binding failure and new-binding success
  + [SBM-006] is visible bounded service and transport faults
  + [SBM-007] is unchanged one-tool metadata and authority
  + [SBM-008] is embedded rollback

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is seven-fold
  + [fold_1_subject] is make Cantor useful to Codex as one basic tool
  + [fold_2_boundary] is adapter backend only while semantics and lifecycle authority remain elsewhere
  + [fold_3_data] is startup mode, pinned client, status response, execute request, service response, ProtocolResponse, and adapter fault
  + [fold_4_governance] is source preservation, mutual exclusion, token secrecy, startup readiness, exact delegation, request binding, and rollback
  + [fold_5_solution] is ServiceClient, backend enum, strict main arguments, equivalence tests, live process test, docs, and proof
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is silent retarget, token leak, unavailable service, bad auth, stale request, wrong result, schema drift, and embedded regression
  + [fold_7_lock] is one read-only query_sop tool with two operator-selected execution backends

